# RFC6154. Junk is where a message goes to be forgotten, so putting
# one there takes it out of every other mailbox its owner has, all
# mail included. A plain COPY does that, not just MOVE: that is how a
# client without MOVE marks spam.
depends allmail
send 1
e create "Junk" (use (\Junk))
receive 1
e OK done
send 1
f select inbox
receive 9
* OK [CLOSED] I, missa est
* 20 EXISTS
* 20 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 21] next uid
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
* OK [UIDVALIDITY 1] uid validity
* OK [MAILBOXID (f...)] stable mailbox ID
f OK [READ-WRITE] done
send 1
g copy 2 Junk
receive 2
* 2 EXPUNGE
g OK [COPYUID 1 2 1] done
send 1
h select Junk
receive 9
* OK [CLOSED] I, missa est
* 1 EXISTS
* 1 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 2] next uid
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
* OK [UIDVALIDITY 1] uid validity
* OK [MAILBOXID (f...)] stable mailbox ID
h OK [READ-WRITE] done
send 1
i select All
receive 9
* OK [CLOSED] I, missa est
* 19 EXISTS
* 0 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 21] next uid
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
* OK [UIDVALIDITY 1] uid validity
* OK [MAILBOXID (f...)] stable mailbox ID
i OK [READ-WRITE] done
send 1
j select inbox
receive 9
* OK [CLOSED] I, missa est
* 19 EXISTS
* 0 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 21] next uid
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
* OK [UIDVALIDITY 1] uid validity
* OK [MAILBOXID (f...)] stable mailbox ID
j OK [READ-WRITE] done
end
